{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TkKFAzwdjd3xxnxpvanpLW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intervals.icu API workout_doc hr target \"units\" \"%lthr\" \"start\" \"end\" instant HR Garmin\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"pkg.go.dev\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tomdiekmann/icu\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"}]\n\nThe search turned up mostly community forum posts, not official Intervals.icu API docs, so treat these as anecdotal.\n\n- **Edge 840 bug:** A forum report says HR-bpm targets pushed via the API on Garmin Edge 840 firmware 30.18 and later get read as a percentage of max HR. In one example, a 122 bpm floor showed as about 242 bpm. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090))\n- **HR targets lost on export:** The same report says the `hr_zone` variant is stripped in `.fit` and `.mrc` exports. It also says Intervals.icu's Zwift importer replaces HR steps with a 0% FTP power target. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090))\n- **Older API limit:** An older developer thread says HR workout editing via the API supported only %HR at the time, and that absolute HR would need the athlete's max HR or LTHR. Later posts say `lthr` and `max_hr` fields were added to the athlete data. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7))\n- **Resolved ranges:** Intervals.icu converts fixed targets into ranges. The default HR range is 1.5%, adjustable with an `hrRange` query parameter, and 0 disables it. Devices alert when the athlete is outside the range. Resolved steps expose `start`/`end` fields, which is a `_power`-style pattern shown for power, not confirmed for HR. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389), [forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129))\n- **Download endpoint:** Event downloads use `/api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/{eventId}/download{ext}`. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7))\n\nNot found: an official schema for HR `units` values, what `instant` means, or how Garmin devices map HR units. Check the Intervals.icu API docs and the developer's own forum posts for those.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e664b5f-577b-4c82-8c3a-823503f5d184","uuid":"cc4bcb7e-008a-4fc1-8975-6b68ab73fa5c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:55:15.594Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Intervals.icu API workout_doc hr target \"units\" \"%lthr\" \"start\" \"end\" instant HR Garmin","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VMh1KoWbbdFgCUvDVzdn6M","content":[{"title":"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20"},{"title":"pkg.go.dev","url":"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tomdiekmann/icu"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609"},{"title":"Workout builder","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md"}]},"The search turned up mostly community forum posts, not official Intervals.icu API docs, so treat these as anecdotal.\n\n- **Edge 840 bug:** A forum report says HR-bpm targets pushed via the API on Garmin Edge 840 firmware 30.18 and later get read as a percentage of max HR. In one example, a 122 bpm floor showed as about 242 bpm. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090))\n- **HR targets lost on export:** The same report says the `hr_zone` variant is stripped in `.fit` and `.mrc` exports. It also says Intervals.icu's Zwift importer replaces HR steps with a 0% FTP power target. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090))\n- **Older API limit:** An older developer thread says HR workout editing via the API supported only %HR at the time, and that absolute HR would need the athlete's max HR or LTHR. Later posts say `lthr` and `max_hr` fields were added to the athlete data. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7))\n- **Resolved ranges:** Intervals.icu converts fixed targets into ranges. The default HR range is 1.5%, adjustable with an `hrRange` query parameter, and 0 disables it. Devices alert when the athlete is outside the range. Resolved steps expose `start`/`end` fields, which is a `_power`-style pattern shown for power, not confirmed for HR. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389), [forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129))\n- **Download endpoint:** Event downloads use `/api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/{eventId}/download{ext}`. ([forum.intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7))\n\nNot found: an official schema for HR `units` values, what `instant` means, or how Garmin devices map HR units. Check the Intervals.icu API docs and the developer's own forum posts for those."],"durationSeconds":8.210370041000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TkKFAzwdjd3xxnxpvanpLW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
